  "sharing_rule": "Exact original reference and rendered presentation. Existing external portrait family aliases omit only unused fallback ornaments; project atlases remain strict.",
  "authoring_instructions": "{\"original_sheet\":\"Create a complete articulated 2D isometric RPG sprite animation atlas based STRICTLY on the attached original ogre image. Preserve this exact original character: massive broad-shouldered muscular olive-green hairless ogre, hunched posture, its original face and heavy jaw, brown ragged leather waist garment, its specific bracers and boots, and the ONE heavy club-like weapon with the small green light shown in the original. Match the weapon's silhouette; do not substitute a sword or add a shield, armor, horns or extra weapons. Match the original small detailed hand-painted game art and elevated isometric camera. No redesign. Fully transparent RGBA background, no scenery, no shadows, no grid or labels. Portrait sheet. EXACTLY EIGHT COLUMNS and THIRTEEN ROWS, exactly 104 separate whole-body poses. Every column must keep one direction throughout, ordered left to right: E facing screen-right in profile; SE facing front-right; S full front toward viewer; SW facing front-left; W screen-left profile; NW back-left; N full back with no face visible; NE back-right. Especially make E versus W and north versus south genuinely different proper views. Keep character scale consistent throughout. EACH POSE occupies only about 55 percent of its cell width and height, leave large fully transparent gutters on all sides and a wide transparent outside margin. Never touch neighbors, never clip weapon or body at a cell edge. EXACT row actions, top to bottom: row 1 idle neutral; row 2 idle breathing raised chest; row 3 walking left leg ahead; row 4 walking passing stance with legs together; row 5 walking right leg ahead; row 6 attack windup with existing heavy weapon drawn back; row 7 attack contact with weapon swung out in the direction the character faces; row 8 attack recovery, pulling weapon back; row 9 hit recoil shoulders jerk back; row 10 hit recovery slightly bowed; row 11 death buckling knees; row 12 death falling sideways toward ground; row 13 final motionless collapsed corpse lying entirely flat. Articulate the original body, limbs and weapon for real distinct poses. Do not duplicate poses, do not merely move a still image, do not add explosion effects. Keep the exact same character and exactly one weapon in all 104 poses.\",\"spacing_correction\":\"Edit the layout of this transparent sprite sheet: MAKE EVERY OGRE SPRITE SIXTY PERCENT OF ITS CURRENT SIZE RELATIVE TO ITS CELL. The sprites must become noticeably smaller on the overall sheet, leaving MUCH more empty transparent space. Keep the same total canvas size and exact 8-column by 13-row grid, exactly 104 poses; each pose stays at the same cell center, but is visibly smaller. Do not preserve the present crowded packing. Preserve the exact ogre design, original details and colors, face, single weapon, viewing directions and all thirteen different actions; ONLY relative sprite size and spacing should change. Each complete sprite including extended club or flat corpse occupies at most sixty percent of cell width, never touches neighboring sprites, with at least twenty-five empty transparent pixels between bodies in every row. Fully transparent background with no labels, grid, effects or scenery. Every character and club remains entirely inside the cell. Preserve north/back and south/front views and pose order.\"}",
